# Proteus Implementation Conventions

## Read the owning SI section first

Before implementing or modifying any module, read the SI section it implements
(`docs/Proteus/paper_1_foundational/SI.tex`). Module and function docstrings must cite
the owning section, e.g. `"""Scale-grid search controller for Stage 1 (SI S2.5.1)."""`.
If the SI is ambiguous or underdetermined for what you need, stop and record the gap in
`OPEN_ISSUES.md` rather than inventing an undocumented heuristic.

## Style (follow existing modules, e.g. rates.py, moments.py, controller.py)

- Pure functions over `numpy` arrays; state in plain dataclasses; configuration in
  `@dataclass(frozen=True)` config objects with defaulted fields.
- `from __future__ import annotations`; type hints throughout; no heavy dependencies
  beyond numpy/scipy without discussion.

## Constants

No new inline magic numbers. Every new constant must be (a) a named, defaulted config
field, (b) classified derived / calibrated / operational (see repo-workflow rule), and
(c) reflected in SI S14.3 or flagged in `OPEN_ISSUES.md` (#37 constant audit). Empirically
tuned values found during debugging are allowed only with a comment naming them as
operational defaults and an issue entry.

## Canonical types

Shared dataclasses (`NodeState`, `Link`, and the SI-contract shapes) live in
`code/proteus/src/proteus/types.py` (promoted out of the test tree, issue #38 resolved).
Import them from `proteus.types`; the `tests/contracts/*` modules are thin re-export
shims that preserve the SI-section grouping for test authors. Do not create duplicate
type definitions — add new canonical shapes to `proteus/types.py` (or a per-module home)
and re-export from the matching `tests/contracts` shim if a contract surface is wanted.

## Flipping awaiting tests

When a module lands, find its `@awaiting("<module key>", si=...)` tests
(`tests/harness/markers.py`), remove the decorator, replace placeholder bodies with real
assertions, and run that marker subset. Never leave a landed module with strict-xfail
tests still pointing at it.

## Environment

`pipenv` from `code/proteus/`; editable install (`pip install -e .[test]`). Default test
run excludes `real_data` and `slow`. See the proteus-testing rule for markers and
reporting format.
